The disk shader cache on Horizon. Upstream compiles it out there (devkitPro's meson change);
disk_cache.c needs mmap, flock, getpwuid, zlib and a file per entry. src/util/disk_cache_switch.c
keeps disk_cache.h's API in one append-only file, $MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR/mesa_shader_cache.bin
(CRC per entry, stale or damaged data discarded; see the file's comment). nouveau names its driver
build with MESA_SWITCH_CACHE_ID (include/mesa_switch_cache_id.h, generated by
scripts/switch/build_mesa.sh from the source and patch hashes) instead of dladdr's build-id. With
the cache, GL_NUM_PROGRAM_BINARY_FORMATS becomes 1 and the GLSL cache skips compile and link.
A host build selects the backend with -DMESA_DISK_CACHE_SINGLE_FILE (switch/mesa/test).

